description:
Write two attributes and a validator that works on any object:

- `[Required]`: the property must not be `null`, and a string must not be empty or only whitespace.
- `[Range(min, max)]`: an `int` property must be between `min` and `max` inclusive.
- `public static class Validator` with `public static List<string> Check(object obj)` returning one message per problem, in the order of the properties as declared, in the forms `"Name is required"` and `"Age must be between 0 and 150"`. A valid object gives an empty list.

```csharp
public class SignUp
{
    [Required] public string? Name { get; set; }
    [Range(13, 120)] public int Age { get; set; }
}

Validator.Check(new SignUp { Name = " ", Age = 7 });
// ["Name is required", "Age must be between 13 and 120"]
```

